# NervAOSP

## Getting Started

NervAOSP is based on LineageOS (Android 16), so you should start from a
LineageOS-compatible device tree.

### Download the Source

Initialize the repo:

```bash
repo init -u https://github.com/NervAOSP/Manifest.git -b 16.2 --git-lfs --depth 1
```

Then sync:

```bash
repo sync -c --force-sync --no-clone-bundle --no-tags -j$(nproc)
```

### Set up Build Environment

```bash
. b*/env*
```

---

## Building NervAOSP

### Choose Device

Select your device target:

```bash
unit lineage_<codename>-bp4a-user
```

Build type defaults to `userdebug` if omitted, for example:

```bash
unit lineage_courbet-bp4a-userdebug
```

### Build the ROM

Compile (this also packages the flashable zip):

```bash
fly -j$(nproc --all)
```

The output zip is named `NervAOSP-Eva-01-<date>-<device>.zip`.

---

## Google Mobile Services (GMS)

NervAOSP supports build-time integrated GMS (the same prebuilt GApps used by
AxionOS, pulled from `vendor/gms`). The flavor is selected per-device by
setting `NERV_VAR` in the device makefile (`lineage_<codename>.mk`) **before**
inheriting the common product config:

```make
# In lineage_<codename>.mk
NERV_VAR := full      # Full Google Mobile Services
# NERV_VAR := pico    # Minimal Google Mobile Services
# NERV_VAR := core    # Core Google Mobile Services
# NERV_VAR := vanilla # Non-GMS build (default)
```

Available `NERV_VAR` values:

| `NERV_VAR` | Result |
| --- | --- |
| `full` | Full Google Mobile Services (GMS) |
| `pico` | Minimal Google Mobile Services |
| `core` | Core Google Mobile Services |
| `vanilla` | Non-GMS build (default when unset) |

Optional GMS package flags (overridable from your device/product makefile):

```make
# Telecom-related Google apps/services bundle.
# Defaults: false for pico, true for core/full.
TARGET_INCLUDE_GOOGLE_TELECOMM := true/false

# Google setup/partner setup bundle.
# Defaults: false for pico/core, true for full.
TARGET_INCLUDE_PARTNER_SETUP := true/false
```

The build flavor shown in the output zip/version is one of `GMS`, `PICO`,
`CORE`, or `VANILLA`, for example:

- `NervAOSP-Eva-01-20260903-GMS-codename.zip` for `full`
- `NervAOSP-Eva-01-20260903-codename.zip` for `vanilla`
